  "scientific_interpretation": [
    "A reduced lower-zone-focused LARE frontier transfers from fixed zero-head forcing to a fresh blind fixed-domain dynamic prescribed-head workload under the pre-existing D13 integrated-water-depth Reference policy.",
    "All reduced lower-zone ladder members R3 through R12 cross the 2x80 cm R2 comparator on both preregistered vectors. The formal R2-relative minimum is R3.",
    "That R3 minimum is not an absolute sufficiency claim. R2 is a weak dynamic-head comparator in this workload: it has 93 bottom-flux sign mismatches and misses the Reference reversal sequence in three of four histories.",
    "The lower-zone ladder shows strong resolution improvement from R3 through R8. R8, R12 and R16 have nearly identical storage and bottom-flux errors, while mapped-profile error still decreases from R8 to R12/R16.",
    "Placement transfers as a real representation variable. R4 is componentwise no worse than U4 and R8 is componentwise no worse than U8 on the dynamic groundwater vector. Uniform U4/U8 each miss reversal sequences in three histories.",
    "Because C4Z has no independently authorized dynamic-head FMC comparator and no application threshold, it does not establish a universal minimum layer count or application acceptance.",
    "The workload contains no top-boundary perturbation, ET or root uptake, so lower-zone placement evidence must not be generalized to surface-driven purposes."
  ],
